  "raw_text": "302\n\nPresent Participles / Participio Presente\n\nThe present particple i\ns usually formed by adding “\ni\n” to the root of the verb\n \n/\n\nLa\n \nparticipio presente\n \ngeneralmente se forma agregando \"\ni\n\" a la raíz del verbo\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nWalaia\n \n–\n \nto listen\n \n/ escuchar\n \n→\n \nWali\n \n–\n \nlisteni\nng\n \n/ escucha\nndo\n\nPlapaia\n \n–\n \nto run\n \n/ correr\n \n→\n \nPlapi\n \n–\n \nrunning\n \n/ corriendo\n\nExceptions/Excepciones:\n\nKaia\n \n–\n \nto be\n \n/ ser, estar\n \n→\n \nSi\n \n–\n \nbeing\n \n/ siendo\n\nWaia\n \n–\n \nto go\n \n/ ir\n \n→\n \nWih\n \n–\n \ngoing\n \n/ yendo\n\nAlternate Spelling/Ortografía alternativa:\n\nDiaia\n \n→\n \nDi\n,\n \nDih\n\nPiaia\n \n→\n \nPi\n,\n \nPih\n\nContinuous Forms / Formas Continuas\n\nUse the present participle combined with the verb\n \nKaia\n \nin the conjugation you wish to use /\n\nUse el participio presente combinado con el verbo\n \nKaia\n \nen la conjugación que desea usar\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nNa minit, kwala tuski sna\n \n–\n \nI am washing clothes\n \nright now\n \n/ Estoy lavando ropa ahora\n\nNahuala titan sut, kwala tuski kapri\n \n–\n \nYesterday, I was washing clothes all morning\n \n/ Ayer estuve lavando ropa toda la\n\nmañana\n\nYauhka tutni sut, kwala tuski\n \nkamna\n \n–\n \nTomorrow, I will be washing clothes all afternoon\n \n/ Mañana estaré\n \nlavando\n \nropa\n\ntoda la tarde\n\nNa minit, kwala tuski sma\n \n–\n \nYou are washing clothes right now\n \n/\n \nEstás lavando ropa ahora\n\nNahuala titan sut, kwala tuski kapram\n \n–\n \nYesterday, you were washing clothes all morning\n \n/\n \nAyer estuviste lavando\n\nropa toda la mañana\n\nYauhka tutni sut, kwala tuski kama\n \n–\n \nTomorrow, you will be washing clothes all afternoon\n \n/\n \nMañana serás lavando\n\nropa toda la tarde\n\nNa minit, kwala tuski sa\n \n–\n \nHe is washing clothes right now\n \n/\n \nEl esta lavando ropa ahora\n\nNahuala\n \ntitan sut, kwala tuski kan\n \n–\n \nYesterday, he was washing clothes all morning\n \n/\n \nAyer estuvo lavando ropa toda la\n\nmañana\n\nYauhka tutni sut, kwala tuski kabia\n \n–\n \nTomorrow, he will be washing clothes all afternoon\n \n/\n \nMañana será lavando ropa\n\ntoda la tarde",
